  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Added:\n- Output schemas and structured content: a generated tool advertises its action's success response type as its outputSchema and returns a successful call's body as structuredContent. Off via \"structuredOutput\": false in generator.json.\n- Tool annotations: every generated tool states readOnlyHint, destructiveHint, idempotentHint and openWorldHint explicitly, derived from its scope and HTTP method (read-only for a read scope, but never for PUT, PATCH or DELETE; destructive for PUT, PATCH, DELETE or a delete scope; idempotent when read-only or PUT/DELETE; never open-world). [McpExpose(ReadOnly/Destructive/Idempotent/OpenWorld = ...)] overrides any of them on an action or a whole controller.\n\nChanged:\n- Clients now see each tool's real hints instead of the spec defaults for an omitted hint (destructive, open-world), so a read-only tool may run without the confirmation a client used to ask for. Review the derived values of any POST that is not purely additive, and of any endpoint that reaches outside systems.\n- A generated tool with an output schema now returns Task<object> from InvokeAsync (the response body as a JsonElement on success, the CallToolResult on error) instead of Task<CallToolResult>. Only code that calls generated tools directly is affected; MCP clients get the same text content plus structuredContent.\n- An empty success (a 204) of a tool with an output schema now comes back as structuredContent null and the text \"null\", instead of an empty text.",
